(ned -- SHOULDER FIND, the last step of calibration. Operator 2026-08-03.)
(Everything up to here is ned's own calibration. This step hands the result)
(to Probe Basic and then uses PB's OWN stock routine for the shoulder, which)
(is the only PB-native part of the exercise.)

(WHAT GETS SENT TO PB)
(  #5181/#5182/#5183 -- the tool-setter position PB drives to. These ARE)
(     LinuxCNC's G30 position, which is why G30.1 sets them: park on the)
(     point and record it. No work-to-machine conversion to get wrong.)
(  #3007 -- max Z plunge, 185 mm: the longest tool the operator uses sits)
(     180 mm from the shoulder, so 185 is that plus a margin.)
(  #3010 -- the SHOULDER itself, written by PB's probe_spindle_nose.)

(THE TWO HEIGHTS, which are different and easy to confuse)
(  tool probing starts at puck top + 100 mm: with a probe rod in and touching)
(     the setter, there is then 100 mm of clearance above it. That is the Z)
(     recorded into G30.)
(  the shoulder is probed at X -20 from the puck centre, because the spindle)
(     nose is a ring -- probing on the centreline would meet the taper bore,)
(     not the face.)

(REQUIRES AN EMPTY SPINDLE. The caller checks and refuses; this is the)
(shoulder, so anything in the taper is what would get measured instead.)

o<cal_shoulder> sub
  #<cx>   = #1
  #<cy>   = #2
  #<top>  = #3

  #<xoff>    = -20.0      (shoulder probes off the centreline, onto the face)
  #<zclear>  = 100.0      (tool-probe start height above the puck top)
  #<plunge>  = 185.0      (longest tool is 180 mm from the shoulder)
  #<f_tr>    = 2000.0

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, SHOULDER: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, SHOULDER: no puck centre - run the calibration first)
  o6 endif

  M50 P0

  (--- 1. record the tool-setter position into G30 -----------------------)
  (XY first, then Z, exactly as everywhere else: the head rests over the)
  (puck and Z must not move until it is laterally clear.)
  G90
  G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> F[#<f_tr>]
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<zclear>] F[#<f_tr>]
  G30.1
  (PRINT, SHOULDER: tool-setter position recorded to G30 - X #5181 Y #5182 Z #5183 machine. That is the puck centre at top plus #<zclear> mm.)

  (--- 2. the plunge allowance PB will use ------------------------------)
  #3007 = #<plunge>
  (PRINT, SHOULDER: max plunge #3007 mm sent to PB.)

  (--- 3. over the shoulder probing point -------------------------------)
  G1 X[#<cx> + #<xoff>] Y#<cy> F[#<f_tr>]
  (PRINT, SHOULDER: at X #<xoff> from centre, probing down up to #<plunge> mm. Spindle must be EMPTY.)

  (--- 4. PB\'s own routine. Untouched: it probes straight down from where)
  (--- it stands and writes #3010, the spindle zero height.)
  M64 P3
  G4 P1.5
  o<probe_spindle_nose> call
  M65 P3

  (PRINT, SHOULDER DONE: spindle zero height #3010 mm. PB now has the setter position, the plunge limit and the shoulder - ready for tool length probing.)
  (DEBUG, SHOULDER DONE: #3010 mm - PB ready)

o<cal_shoulder> endsub

M2 (end program)
